<article class="prose support-page">
  <header><p class="eyebrow">We’re here to help</p><h1>Support</h1><p class="lede">Choose the path that best describes the issue. Email is the support channel during the private beta.</p></header>
  <div class="support-grid">
    <section><h2>Product help</h2><p>Include the app platform and version, what you expected, and what happened. Do not send passwords, sign-in codes, or tokens.</p><p><a class="button" href="mailto:info@onmyradar.pro?subject=OnMyRadar%20product%20support">Contact product support</a></p></section>
    <section><h2>Inaccurate event</h2><p>Use the in-app report action when possible. Otherwise include the public event title and source link—never your private Radar text.</p><p><a class="button" href="mailto:info@onmyradar.pro?subject=Inaccurate%20event%20report">Report an event</a></p></section>
    <section><h2>Privacy or account</h2><p>For access, correction, export, or deletion, write from the email associated with your account. We will verify control before disclosing or deleting data.</p><p><a class="button" href="mailto:info@onmyradar.pro?subject=Privacy%20or%20account%20request">Make a privacy request</a></p></section>
    <section id="security"><h2>Security concern</h2><p>Send a concise description and safe reproduction steps. Do not include real customer data, credentials, or exploit public systems. We acknowledge actionable reports as quickly as practical.</p><p><a class="button" href="mailto:info@onmyradar.pro?subject=Security%20report">Report securely by email</a></p></section>
  </div>
  <section class="callout"><h2>Before you write</h2><p>OnMyRadar cannot change an organizer’s schedule, refund a ticket, or guarantee an event. Confirm time, price, availability, accessibility, and cancellation with the original organizer.</p></section>
</article>
